  /// Where the gateway-recovery record lives.
  ///
  /// Empty -- the default -- keeps the compiled, XOR-obfuscated URL, so the
  /// shipping build is unchanged. It exists because the compiled URL's *path*
  /// is `/winsvpn/winsvpn-downloads/`: the host has high blocking collateral,
  /// but the path names the product to GitHub and to anyone holding the APK,
  /// and this is the channel that has to survive the gateway being blocked.
  /// The owner gets one client release, so the rotation channel has to be
  /// settable at build time or it is fixed forever.
  ///
  /// A value that is set but not a usable https URL degrades to **no recovery
  /// fetch at all**, never back to the compiled default -- the same rule
  /// `preVpnGeoEdgeBases` follows, and for the same reason: falling back would
  /// restore the branded path in exactly the build that was replacing it.
  static const String _recoveryRecordUrlOverride = String.fromEnvironment(
    'WINS_RECOVERY_RECORD_URL',
    defaultValue: '',
  );
