const String _kNoticeHevLwip = r'''
hev-socks5-tunnel, and lwIP as embedded by it
Copyright (c) hev.  (hev-socks5-tunnel, MIT)
Copyright (c) Swedish Institute of Computer Science.  (lwIP, BSD-3-Clause)
All rights reserved.

Holders are named from upstream project metadata, not from a licence file in
this tree -- there is none, for the reason given below. No year ranges are
asserted for the same reason.

Declared by: amnezia-vpn/amneziawg-android's `tunnel` module, which resolves
`com.zaneschepke:hevtunnel:1.0.1` as an `implementation` dependency, and which
carries github.com/heiher/hev-socks5-tunnel as the submodule
hevtunnel/src/main/jni/hev-socks5-tunnel.

*** SCOPE FINDING -- THIS COMPONENT WAS NOT FOUND IN ANY SHIPPED ARTIFACT ***
Verified 2026-08-07 against the vendored AAR: android/app/libs/amneziawg.aar
contains only libam-go.so, libam-quick.so, libam.so and classes.jar -- no hev
native library and no hev class. android/app/build.gradle.kts consumes the AAR
through `fileTree`, which does not resolve an AAR's POM transitives, so
`com.zaneschepke:hevtunnel` is never pulled into the app. A repository-wide
search for "hev", "lwip" and "tun2socks" found no source on any platform.

The entry is retained anyway, and deliberately: it costs a user nothing, an
over-inclusive permissive notice harms no one, and a future AAR rebuilt from
upstream's `tunnel` module could pull the dependency in without anyone
noticing. Because no hev or lwIP source is present in this tree, the verbatim
MIT and BSD-3-Clause texts could not be reproduced from a pinned source and
are NOT quoted below. Both must be added from github.com/heiher/
hev-socks5-tunnel and its third-part/lwip subtree if this component is ever
confirmed to ship. lwIP's BSD-3-Clause carries a non-endorsement clause.

Verbatim MIT and BSD-3-Clause texts pending: no hev-socks5-tunnel or lwIP
source is present in this repository to reproduce them from. See the scope
finding above.
''';

